> password</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> dbname </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> dbname</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> host </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> host</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> port </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> port<br>    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    query </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;SELECT * FROM invoices&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    invoices </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> dbGetQuery</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">con</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> query</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    dbDisconnect</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">con</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    invoices<br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>This code was placed in a file (I sourced it in server.R). Actually, I have to open a new connection, query and then close the connection. <br><br>Is there any solution allows Shiny app only use one database connection? <br><br>Thank you in advance. <br></div>"
